---Contains an assessment that GuardDuty derived from the data during an investigation, such as a threat assessment, a comparison against normal behavior, or a process lineage. The record contains at most one of the payload members, the one that corresponds to AnalysisType. Indicators can accompany any analysis type.
---@class aws.guardduty.AnalysisRecord
---@field AnalysisType aws.guardduty.AnalysisType The kind of analysis. The value identifies the payload member that can be set: REPUTATION, THREAT_ASSESSMENT, and RDS_THREAT_ASSESSMENT (ThreatAssessment); KUBERNETES_POLICY_VIOLATION (KubernetesPolicyViolation); S3_EXPOSURE, S3_ACTOR_CONTEXT, and S3_PEN_TEST (S3Analysis); PROCESS_LINEAGE (Processes); and TREND and BASELINE (AccountAnalysis).
---@field ThreatAssessment? aws.guardduty.InvestigationThreatAssessment A threat assessment. Set when AnalysisType is REPUTATION, THREAT_ASSESSMENT, or RDS_THREAT_ASSESSMENT.
---@field KubernetesPolicyViolation? aws.guardduty.KubernetesPolicyViolation An assessment of a Kubernetes policy violation. Set when AnalysisType is KUBERNETES_POLICY_VIOLATION.
---@field S3Analysis? aws.guardduty.S3Analysis An analysis of Amazon S3 activity or exposure. Set when AnalysisType is S3_EXPOSURE, S3_ACTOR_CONTEXT, or S3_PEN_TEST.
---@field Processes? aws.guardduty.Processes The processes in a process lineage. Set when AnalysisType is PROCESS_LINEAGE.
---@field AccountAnalysis? aws.guardduty.InvestigationAccountAnalysis An analysis of the findings in an account over time. Set when AnalysisType is TREND or BASELINE.
---@field Indicators? aws.guardduty.InvestigationIndicators The threat indicators associated with the analysis, such as an IP address, a domain, or a file hash.

---@alias aws.guardduty.AnalysisType "REPUTATION"|"THREAT_ASSESSMENT"|"RDS_THREAT_ASSESSMENT"|"KUBERNETES_POLICY_VIOLATION"|"S3_EXPOSURE"|"S3_ACTOR_CONTEXT"|"S3_PEN_TEST"|"PROCESS_LINEAGE"|"TREND"|"BASELINE"

